# Compiled driver/tool binaries produced at the repo root.
#
# Every entry here MUST be root-anchored with a leading "/". A bare pattern
# matches a basename at ANY depth and matches directories too, so bare
# "test-lease-e2e" also ignores scripts/test-lease-e2e/ — silently swallowing
# any NEW file added under that driver's source directory. Already-tracked
# files are unaffected, which is exactly why the trap stays hidden until it
# bites someone's `git add` as a no-op.
#
# This has cost real time three times: scripts/test-chat-e2e/, the cmd/xe
# package directory (bare "xe" — which is why cmd/xe had no tests at all until
# it was anchored), and this file's own history. Anchor new entries. See #823.
